## Context
Follow-up of ticket 1236 (PR #1755, merged on the author's ruling 2026-10-27 after its final gaze).
The last review found two narrower edges that only a dishonest or careless editor reaches:
1. `criteria_hash` matches `^## Exit criteria\s*$` exactly; `## Exit Criteria`, `### Exit criteria`
   or `## Exit criteria (added)` added after recording read `reused`. Worse: renaming the real heading,
   weakening it, and appending an unchanged copy of the old section also passes. None of 709 closed
   tickets uses a variant heading.
2. If `record` and `gate` both name the same unrelated ticket, the PR's real ticket can be rewritten
   and the gate reads `reused`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The criteria section match is case-insensitive at any heading level (`^#{2,}\s*exit criteria\b`),
      or a ticket whose criteria heading is not exact is refused; tests for the three variants and the
      rename-and-append case read stale or refused, and fail on the code before the fix.
- [ ] The gate compares the recorded ticket with the ticket the PR claims to close and refuses a mismatch.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
scripts/review_evidence.py, tests/test_review_evidence.py, skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md

